<div class="page">
  <h2 style="font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">Flexible Spending Accounts</h2>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">The Medical Spending Account (FSA) – 1/1 to 12/31/21 Plan Year</p>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">The Medical Spending Account is a pre-tax savings account to be used for qualified medical, dental and vision expenses for you and your eligible dependents. Per the IRS, an employee may elect up to $2,750 for the 2021 calendar year. <span data-field="fsa_eligibility_note">{{ fsa_eligibility_note }}</span></p>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">FSA contains a Use It or Lose It provision – plan carefully!</p>

  <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 25px;">Dependent Care Spending Account (DCA) – 1/1/21 to 12/31/21 Plan Year</p>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">The Dependent Care Spending Account is a pre-tax savings account for elder care and child care expenses. You must be using daycare services so that you and your spouse can work. In addition, your provider of care must furnish you with his/her Social Security Number or Tax Identification Number. By law, the maximum amount that you may contribute to any Dependent Care Spending Account for your family is $5,000 each Plan Year. Per the IRS, an employee may elect up to $5,000 for the 2021 calendar year. <span data-field="dca_eligibility_note">{{ dca_eligibility_note }}</span></p>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">DCA contains a Use It or Lose It provision – plan carefully!</p>

  <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 25px;">Limited Purpose Spending Account (LPSA) – 1/1/21 to 12/31/21 Plan Year</p>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">The Limited Purpose Flexible Spending Account is a pre-tax savings account to be used for qualified dental and vision expenses only for you and your eligible dependents. Per the IRS, an employee may elect up to $2,750 for the 2021 calendar year. <span data-field="lpsa_eligibility_note">{{ lpsa_eligibility_note }}</span></p>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">LPSA contains a Use It or Lose It provision – plan carefully!</p>

  <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 25px;">Health Savings Account (HSA) – 1/1/21 to 12/31/21 Plan Year</p>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-bottom: 20px;">The Health Savings Account is a pre-tax savings account to be used for qualified medical, dental and vision expenses for you and your eligible dependents. Per the IRS, an employee may elect up to $3,600 single or $7,200 family for the 2021 calendar year. These limits include funds from Wilkes University and any employee contributions. Employee must be over 26 years of age to be eligible for an HSA. An HSA is not considered taxable income. Important Notice: If you have enrolled in the Health Savings Account and receive funding (employer not another HDHP), you are ineligible to enroll in the Health Savings Account and receive funding (employer and employee).</p>
  <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-bottom: 20px;"><span data-field="hsa_eligibility_note">{{ hsa_eligibility_note }}</span></p>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 20px;">An HSA is not a Use-It-or-Lose-It account.</p>
</div>


